      "message": "With match statement it adds twice nesting to the main line logic, how about with `if let` (see updated CL)? It avoids unwrap and adds only 1 nest to main line.\n\nI wish `let...else` feature (https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/3137-let-else.html) could be used, it could look like this:\n\n```\nlet (Some(name), Some(old_owner), Some(new_owner)) \u003d msg.get3::\u003c...\u003e() else {\n  // Invalid NameOwnerChanged signal, ignore.\n  return true;\n};\n\n// main line goes here without unwrap and nesting.\n```",
